        {
          "text": "Around 95 % of vacancies specify that local language proficiency is required",
          "evidence": [26]
        },
        {
          "text": "Many candidates are filtered out due to lack of local language skills",
          "evidence": [27]
        },
        {
          "text": "Higher education rarely influences hiring decisions",
          "evidence": [32]
        },
        {
          "text": "P3’s salary for the current position was higher than expected, but after negotiating accepted the minimum (still higher than fast‑food wages)",
          "evidence": [37]
        },
        {
          "text": "Typical language requirement for tech positions is B2, sometimes B1, and certificates are usually not demanded",
          "evidence": [46]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": “language‑learning”,
      "title": "Language learning experiences in Slovakia and Austria",
